bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    mir_declaration_field_offset_identity_mismatch_2026_11_14, 0, "2026-11-26 verified on aarch64 NVIDIA GB10 (cc 12.1, driver 580.173.02) with seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-wr-seed1126b/release/simple: test/02_integration/gpu/cuda_struct_field_layout_live_spec.spl lowers struct Pair(small,wide), struct RevPair(wide,small) and class PairBox(small,wide) through the real MirLowering (all wide@0 small@8 stride16), compiles GEP/SetField/GetField kernels with the plugin CudaBackend, runs them on the device and compares every byte with host-computed values incl. untouched padding: Pair=0 RevPair=0 PairBox=0 mismatches, 2/2 examples pass (2 runs)."
    mir_declaration_field_offset_identity_mismatch_2026_11_14, 1, "Sabotage red on the device: reverting both lowerers to layout.fields[fi].offset gives Pair=640 RevPair=0 PairBox=640 device mismatches (RevPair declaration order equals physical order). Device verification first required cuda_field_access_hardcoded_local_state_space_2026_11_26 (GetField/SetField emitted st.local on global pointers: CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS 700)."
    mir_declaration_field_offset_identity_mismatch_2026_11_14, 2, "Unit evidence: layout_field_identity_v1_spec 3/3, cuda_layout_extent_v1_spec 3/3; mir_exported_types_spec struct+class field-identity examples pass after repairing Span/LayoutKind import drift (5 unrelated examples still fail: is_global nil field at :121 and removed BootstrapHirModuleOwner). Scope: kernels are hand-built MIR over the real lowered type table; source-level [Struct] kernels are still rejected by the CUDA backend (local Struct type)."

